\ Freeze-time call-site inference narrows parameters the user did not annotate.
\
\ No word here declares a parameter type. Every call site passes a literal, so the
\ freeze-time pass proves each parameter and codegen unboxes it at entry. The
\ arithmetic then compiles concretely and the comparison takes the inline path.
\
\ Build-only: the golden is the --compilation-stats report. Without the inference
\ table this program records six fallbacks; with it only the two `.` -> inspect
\ sites the prelude always emits survive.

diff: ( a b -- r ) [ - ] ;
below?: ( a b -- r ) [ < ] ;

\ Self-tail-recursive: the back-edge rewrites the parameter slots each iteration,
\ so a fallback-free `+` here is what pins that the narrowing is re-read inside the
\ loop region rather than only at first entry. Float, because a fixnum sum is
\ provable only under the lock -- fixnum arithmetic can promote to bignum, so the
\ pass refuses to type its result unless the build rejects the promoting path.
fsum-to: ( acc n -- r ) [
  dup 0.0 = [ drop ] [ swap over + swap 1.0 - fsum-to ] if
] ;

10 4 diff .
3 4 below? .
0.0 100.0 fsum-to .
